  "interpretation": [
    "On four frozen visible-intent points both builds produced zero correct first-turn pins and zero correct choices. V5 proposed one unrelated selectable stall on R02; v6 offered none. The three clear-access point intents provide the same zero-of-three result. The remaining R01 identifies a real visual destination with uncertain vehicle access.",
    "V5 completed an evidence-based withholding on one of three blocked natural requests; v6 did so on two. Neither version offered an incorrect point or choice on a blocked natural request. Wording on the v6 traffic-at-the-lights clarification remained generic, and did not cite the active motor lane. The other v6 blocked request timed out.",
    "Both builds withheld seven of seven independent lane marks and all four intended off-lane area marks. The latter measures location availability; a no-pin result on R01 can be sensible when the visible pedestrian strip interrupts access.",
    "V6 native geometry supplied zero target points on all four positive scenes. R02 contributed the only pre-language option on any of the seven scenes, a signed OPEN stall on the left outside the requested position on the right. Rejecting it removed the v5 false choice. The three definite-access misses cannot be remedied by matching more phrasings to the same raw inventory."
  ]
